# Exocortex v1 — Round 2 Review (Audit of Round-1 Closure)

**Status:** CLOSED 2026-08-25. Every item below landed with its verify
clause; `master-plan.prd` tracks the closure map and the v2 deferrals
(D6-D11).

**Method:** deterministic gates re-run fresh, plus four orthogonal reviewers
(milestone-AC auditor, round-1 closure verifier, invariants/security auditor,
architecture/dependency auditor). Every finding below was independently
re-verified against the PRD text and the code before inclusion; each cites
both.

**Baseline (verified fresh, 2026-08-23):**

- `cargo test --workspace` — 106 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` — green
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — green
- `cargo deny check` — green (17 recorded advisory ignores)
- `cargo xtask kernel-purity` / `fingerprint` / `no-llm` — green
  (fingerprint `d8bcd004…4e8c`, unchanged from round 1)
- `cargo xtask bench` — green: search p50 29µs / p99 731µs
  (budgets 500µs/3ms; p99 drifted 680→731µs since round 1, still in budget);
  k-hop p50 269µs / p99 336µs (budgets 300µs/2ms)

## Round-1 closure verdict

Closed with fix AND verify-test (spot-confirmed): **B1, B2, W1, W2, W3, W4,
W5, W6, W8, H3, H4, H5, H7, H8.**

Closed with residue (see H12): **W7** (fix complete, prescribed
kill-the-holder test absent), **H1** (no test), **H2** (ceiling
persist/reload untested), **H6** (bundle: `get_memory_for` is dead code,
`RedisFireQueue` unwired, tag-normalization and `effective_strength`
untested), and the master plan's "Round 1 complete. No open items."
overstates W7 and H6 accordingly.

## Process finding

**P1. The entire round-1 closure is uncommitted.** Git has 11 commits
(`M0`…`M8` + report + lint sweep); every round-1 fix exists only as
uncommitted working-tree modifications and untracked files
(`git status`: 35 modified, 8 untracked, incl. `sync.rs`, `embedding.rs`,
`http_bind.rs`, `backend.rs`, `fire.rs`). Until committed, the round-1
"Done" table in `master-plan.prd` is not reproducible from history.
**Action:** commit the round-1 closure (one commit, message
`round-1: close B1-B2, W1-W8, H1-H8 per round-1-review.prd`) before starting
round-2 work.

