## Phase 4 — Observability (§19)

### W14. `/health/ready` is a constant; `hydrated` hard-coded; metric families missing; OTel absent

- **Where:** `http_bind.rs:110-113` (static `{"status":"ready"}`),
  `backend.rs:134-138` (`hydrated: true` at startup), ~4 of §19's ~17 metric
  families emitted, zero opentelemetry references.
- **PRD:** §19 R-O2 (families incl. ops duration, queue depth/lag, cluster,
  client, cache), R-O3 (OTel traces), R-O4 (ready checks storage/cache/
  worker/cluster).
- **Fix:** wire real readiness (storage ping, cache hydration flag actually
  flipped on reseed completion, worker/cluster status); add the missing
  metric families at the emit points §19 names; scope OTel to a v2 note in
  the report if it stays out (it is currently entirely absent and
  unrecorded).
- **Verify:** test — stop storage (or point at a dead URL): `/health/ready`
  flips within one check interval; `/metrics` contains
  `ops_duration_seconds` after one op.

